./mvnw verify
```

The tests use a fake model: they never call <%= provider.id %> and cost nothing.
<%_ if (features.postgres || features.redis) { _%>
Docker must run: the tests start <%= [features.postgres ? 'Postgres' : '', features.redis ? 'Redis' : ''].filter(Boolean).join(' and ') %> in containers (Testcontainers).
<%_ } _%>
<%_ if (features.evals) { _%>

### Evaluations

```bash
ollama pull <%= evals.model %><%= features.vectorStore && provider.id !== 'ollama' ? ' && ollama pull nomic-embed-text' : '' %>
./mvnw verify -Pevals
```

The whole agent answers on Ollama (`OLLAMA_BASE_URL`, `EVALS_MODEL`, <%= evals.model %> by default)<%= evals.dataset ? `: each case of \`${evals.dataset}\`
is scored by its words and, judged by the model, by its criterion` : '' %><%= features.redTeam ? `${evals.dataset ? ';' : ':'} the red team attacks it in English and French
and checks it neither leaks its instructions nor obeys` : '' %>. The report is in `target/evals-report.md`; the run fails below the
threshold. `.github/workflows/ci.yml` runs the tests, then the evaluations with Ollama, on every push.
<%_ } _%>
<%_ if (features.helm) { _%>

## Kubernetes

`helm/<%= project.artifactId %>` deploys the image built from the Dockerfile:

```bash
<%_   const secretNames = [...secrets, ...(features.postgres ? ['DATABASE_PASSWORD'] : [])]; _%>
<%_   if (secretNames.length > 0) { _%>
kubectl create secret generic <%= project.artifactId %>-secrets <%- secretNames.map((name) => `--from-literal=${name}=...`).join(' ') %>
<%_   } _%>
helm install <%= project.artifactId %> ./helm/<%= project.artifactId %> -f my-values.yaml
```

Secrets are only referenced (`existingSecret`); <%= [features.postgres ? 'Postgres' : '', features.redis ? 'Redis' : '', features.oidc ? 'the identity provider' : ''].filter(Boolean).join(', ') || 'the services' %> run apart, set in `env`
of `values.yaml`. Kubernetes probes liveness and readiness on the management port, which no Service exposes; the
container runs as a non-root user on a read-only file system. An ingress is ready in `values.yaml` (`ingress.enabled`).
<%_ } _%>

